                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1630-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>MXL Tempo XLR</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Tempo XLR is a studio condenser from MXL&#8217;s &#8220;Tempo&#8221; series. It is the first non-USB mic in the series, but retains the line&#8217;s familiar form factor and styling. </p><p>The capsule is described as a 22mm design, but is very likely MXL&#8217;s standard 17mm small-diaphragm design. However, we note that the USB Tempo mic uses an electret capsule, so it is possible the XLR version breaks from MXL&#8217;s traditional capsule choices.</p><p>The circuit is described only as a &#8220;FET preamp;&#8221; we assume it is MXL&#8217;s standard transformerless design. Like the 604 pencil mic, this circuit has a switchable 10dB pad.</p><p>The Tempo XLR ships with a ring mount and polishing cloth.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/MXL/Tempo-XLR">MXL Tempo-XLR</a></p>
